VTID-04272 — commands run to build and verify this change

1. Queried live Supabase (`autopilot_recommendations`, `dev_autopilot_config`,
   `dev_autopilot_executions`) to confirm the real backlog size (18 rows,
   not the Command Hub's "30 NEW FINDINGS" aggregate stat) and to identify
   the one `auto_exec_eligible:true` finding — `9e1bdb97-d4ec-449d-a00b-
   5ec70428cada` ("CVE: package.json") — and its prior failure history
   (5+ failed agent-executor attempts, stranded PR #3543).

2. `cd services/gateway && npm audit --omit=dev 2>&1 | tail -20` (and the
   full, non---omit=dev run) — baseline: 41 vulnerabilities
   (2 low, 14 moderate, 21 high, 4 critical).

3. `cd services/gateway && npm audit fix` (non-force)
   -> `git status --short` confirmed only `package-lock.json` changed
      (947 lines: 608 insertions, 339 deletions); `package.json` untouched.
   -> Re-ran `npm audit`: 16 vulnerabilities remaining (9 moderate, 7 high),
      all 4 criticals resolved (handlebars, protobufjs, sanitize-html,
      websocket-driver). Remaining 16 all require a major version bump
      (firebase-admin, @anthropic-ai/sdk, sharp) — deliberately deferred,
      not attempted in this pass (AC-1).

4. `cd services/gateway && npx tsc --noEmit` -> clean, no output.

5. `cd services/gateway && npx jest --silent` -> 97 test suites FAILED:
   `SyntaxError: Cannot use import statement outside a module` at
   `node_modules/sanitize-html/node_modules/htmlparser2/dist/index.js:1`.

6. Root-caused: step 3's audit fix bumped sanitize-html's own recorded
   dependency on htmlparser2 from ^10.1.0 (CJS) to ^12.0.0 (ESM-only,
   "type":"module"), nested at
   node_modules/sanitize-html/node_modules/htmlparser2/ (npm did not hoist
   it, because a different top-level consumer still needs the older,
   CJS-compatible version at node_modules/htmlparser2/).

   Confirmed NOT a production runtime bug:
   `node -e "require('sanitize-html')"` -> works fine (Node's own
   package.json "exports"/CJS interop resolves it). This is purely a Jest
   transform-config gap — Jest's default config skips transforming
   node_modules/ files, and the pre-existing transformIgnorePatterns regex
   only matched an allow-listed package name appearing immediately after
   the FIRST node_modules/ segment in a path, so an unanchored .test()
   against the nested path matched (at the "sanitize-html" segment, via
   the alternation group itself) before ever reaching "htmlparser2" deeper
   in the string.

7. Verified the fix in isolation first with a standalone Node script
   (scratchpad, not committed) before touching the real file:
   `new RegExp("node_modules/(?!(.*/)?(\\.pnpm/)?(node-fetch|...|htmlparser2|...)/)")`
   -> confirmed: matches false (WILL transform) on both the top-level and
      the nested sanitize-html/node_modules/htmlparser2 path; matches true
      (WILL ignore) on an unrelated package (lodash) at any depth.

8. Applied the verified fix to `services/gateway/jest.config.js`'s
   `transformIgnorePatterns` — added an optional `(.*/)? ` group before
   the `(\\.pnpm/)?` group and a trailing `/` after the alternation.

9. `cd services/gateway && npx jest --silent` -> 1058/1059 suites (1
   pre-existing skip), 17,283/17,318 tests passing, 0 failures. All 97
   previously-failing suites now pass.

10. `cd services/gateway && npx tsc --noEmit` -> clean again after the
    jest.config.js edit.

11. `git status --short` -> also showed `specs/command-hub-symbol-index.json`
    modified (a side effect of one of the test suites invoking its own
    generator script, `scripts/generate-command-hub-symbol-index.mjs`,
    unrelated to this VTID) — reverted with
    `git checkout -- specs/command-hub-symbol-index.json` to keep this
    commit scoped to the CVE fix (AC-1/AC-2).

12. Wrote `services/gateway/test/vtid-04272-jest-transform-ignore-nested-
    node-modules.test.ts` (5 tests) pinning the exact real-world regression:
    a top-level allow-listed package still transforms, the nested
    sanitize-html/node_modules/htmlparser2 path now transforms (the actual
    bug), a pnpm-nested path transforms, an unrelated package (lodash) at
    any depth is still ignored, and the raw pattern source requires the
    trailing-slash/optional-prefix shape.

13. `cd services/gateway && node node_modules/.bin/jest
    test/vtid-04272-jest-transform-ignore-nested-node-modules.test.ts`
    -> 5/5 passing.

14. Mutation verification: temporarily reverted jest.config.js's
    transformIgnorePatterns to the pre-fix (buggy) regex, re-ran the new
    test file -> 3 of 5 tests correctly FAILED (proving the test catches
    the regression), then restored the fix and re-ran -> 5/5 passing again.

15. `cd services/gateway && npx tsc --noEmit` (final) -> clean, no output.

16. `cd services/gateway && npx jest --silent` (final, with the new test
    file included) -> 1059/1060 suites (1 pre-existing skip), 17,288/17,323
    tests passing (29 skipped, 6 todo, both pre-existing), 0 failures,
    42/42 snapshots passing.

No AWS/GCP/Supabase mutation was made from this session for this VTID
beyond the initial read-only queries in step 1. Marking the
`autopilot_recommendations` rows resolved and closing stranded PR #3543
are deliberately left for after this PR merges and deploys (see
